            <ArticleTitle>Endoscopic management of a case of 'complete septate uterus with unilateral haematometra'.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2171-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Endoscopy and ultrasound was used to diagnose a 13 year old virgin girl who presented with dysmenorrhoea and suspected right side adnexal tumescence. The girl was found to have a complete septate uterus with non-communicating right hemicavity and haematometra, an exceptional type of Müllerian anomaly. After pretreatment with buserelin, hysteroscopic metroplasty was successfully performed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
